#
# LLM runtime configuration for InferNode.
#
# lib/ndb/llm is git-ignored so a developer's endpoints, models, and
# gateway URLs stay local. This file is the tracked template.
#
# You normally do NOT need to copy it by hand:
#   - lib/sh/profile seeds $home/.infernode/lib/ndb/llm from this
#     template on first run when no config exists yet;
#   - the Settings app and llmctl write the seeded copy thereafter;
#   - setup-macos.sh / setup-linux.sh write it during guided setup;
#   - release artifacts ship their own distribution defaults.
#
# Ship this file BLANK. lucibridge treats a set url= as "already
# configured" and skips the first-run setup wizard, so a stray value
# here sends a fresh install straight to an endpoint that does not
# exist on the user's machine, with no way through the UI to fix it.
#
# Fields:
#   mode     local | remote
#              local  — talk to a backend on this machine (or a URL)
#              remote — mount a remote llmsrv over 9P (see dial=)
#   backend  api | openai | cli
#              api    — Anthropic API (url=https://api.anthropic.com)
#              openai — any OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, SGLang, …)
#              cli    — a local Claude CLI gateway
#   url      backend endpoint, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#   model    model name to request, e.g. mistral-small3.2:24b
#   dial     remote mode only: 9P dial string, e.g. tcp!host!5640
#
# Optional:
#   auth        keyring (remote mode, authenticated mount)
#   keyfile     path to the keyring file used by auth=keyring
#   temperature per-deployment sampling temperature override
#
mode=local
backend=
url=
model=
dial=
